# NAME: ProxySupplement
# AUTHOR: UykiZhao
# REPO: https://github.com/UykiZhao/Clash-Party-Override-Rule
# UPDATED: 2026-09-22
# PURPOSE: DNS leak guard extras. Foreign DoH endpoints, leak-test mirrors and
#          public resolver IPs are forced through the proxy so apps with
#          hardcoded DNS cannot bypass the hijack. Domestic DoH endpoints are
#          intentionally excluded - proxying them would break CN CDN results.
#          Leak-test/VPN sites mirror the prevent_dns_leak ruleset referenced
#          by the Clash YAML overrides.

# Leak-test mirrors and VPN/provider domains (xishang0128 prevent_dns_leak)
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,vpnunlimited.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,whrq.net
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,whoer.net
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,perfect-privacy.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,pixelscan.net
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,ping0.cc
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,ipapi.co
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,adspower.net
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,expressvpn.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,nordvpn.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,surfshark.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,surfsharkdns.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,astrill.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,astrill.org
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,dnsleak.asn247.net

# Foreign encrypted DNS endpoints
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,doh.cleanbrowsing.org
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,dns.adguard-dns.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,dns.nextdns.io
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,doh.mullvad.net
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,dns.controld.com

# Public resolver IPs: catches DoH/DoT straight to IP (hijack-dns covers :53)
IP-CIDR,1.1.1.1/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,1.0.0.1/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,8.8.8.8/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,8.8.4.4/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,9.9.9.9/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,149.112.112.112/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,208.67.222.222/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,208.67.220.220/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,94.140.14.14/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,94.140.15.15/32,no-resolve
